# Patch: fix quickjs_rs Wasmtime thread affinity (complements the _engine.py fix)
#
# Target: quickjs_rs/context.py (PyPI package quickjs-rs==0.2.6)
#
# The _engine.py fix (fix-quickjs-wasmtime-cross-thread-crash.patch) prevents
# the trampoline from crashing when _CUR.inst is None. But it does NOT fix
# the underlying problem: the Wasmtime Store is NOT thread-safe. When a
# js_eval script calls task(), the subagent's Wasmtime work runs on a
# different thread (the outer LangGraph loop). Any Store access from that
# thread (resolve_pending, reject_pending, eval, etc.) raises
# WasmtimeError: An internal error occurred.
#
# This patch adds thread affinity to quickjs_rs/context.py:
#   - _wasmtime_affinity: the thread that created the context (first to touch
#     the store).
#   - _on_wasmtime_thread(fn): if the caller is on the affinity thread, run
#     fn() inline (zero overhead). Otherwise, serialize fn() onto a single
#     persistent affinity thread via a queue, so the store is always touched
#     by exactly ONE OS thread for its lifetime.
#   - All Store access points in Context are wrapped with _on_wasmtime_thread.
#
# How to apply:
#   cd <your-dcode-install>/lib/python3.14/site-packages
#   patch -p1 < /path/to/fix-quickjs-wasmtime-thread-affinity.patch
#
# NOTE: apply the _engine.py patch FIRST (it is a prerequisite — without it,
# the trampolines crash before the affinity hop can take effect).

